{
  "_doc": [
    "The shell's themes: the one registry read by the shell (modules/common/Themes.qml),",
    "the Nix options (lib.nix: `appearance.theme` and each `appearance.<id>.variant` are enums of",
    "these ids), the login screen (scripts/theme-palettes.py, greeter.nix) and niri's first frames.",
    "`default` is the theme when none is set; a theme's `defaultVariant` (else its first) is its default variant.",
    "A theme's `style` (a variant's own overriding it) is its look as data: see Themes.qml.",
    "A variant's `palette` (optional) replaces the wallpaper-generated Material palette while the",
    "theme is on (MaterialThemeLoader). A variant's (or theme's) `wallpaper` (optional, a path in the shell tree) is",
    "shown when switching to it until the user picks another (services/ThemeWallpapers.qml).",
    "`sounds` ({notification, critical}: the chime, and the critical notification's sound; {focus, countdown, alarm}:",
    "the timers' ringtones) at the top level are the defaults; a theme's or a variant's own override them",
    "(Themes.sound). On every theme but the default they replace the user's sound settings (Audio.soundFor).",
    "Paths are in the shell tree.",
    "See README.md \"Themes\" for adding one."
  ],
  "default": "material",
  "sounds": {
    "notification": "assets/sounds/persona5-notification.mp3",
    "critical": "assets/sounds/persona5-cut-in.mp3"
  },
